  "finish_attachment": {
    "top_tile_method": "one small centered dot of removable neutral-cure silicone per tile on sealed plywood; qualify on PETG and the actual finish, keep every perimeter and 0.6 mm seam free to move, and remove with floss rather than prying",
    "rear_curb_method": "one field-drilled clearance slot per straight curb piece and one per arm of the corner replacement, using short nonstructural pan-head screws into plywood after a bottom-clearance check; do not clamp PETG rigidly",
    "fascia_method": "the full-depth upper and lower channel flanges mechanically capture the fascia around the real shelf stack; assemble the lateral train before the two outer endcaps and re-entrant corner cover, then use one tiny centered removable neutral-cure silicone dot inside each channel only to prevent creep and rattle; do not drill or notch the continuous steel angle",
    "entablature_overlay_method": "one tiny centered removable neutral-cure silicone dot to its own fascia half after the actual PETG surfaces pass the adhesion and floss-removal coupon; no overlay may bridge a 0.6 mm fascia seam",
    "keystone_method": "two pinhead-size removable neutral-cure silicone dots on one arch half only; the opposite side floats across the 0.6 mm center seam",
    "groin_vault_method": "two generated clearance slots and short nonstructural pan-head screws into the underside of the through-owned plywood only after a depth stop and bracket-clearance check; never bridge the plywood joint",
    "corner_pilaster_method": "two tiny removable neutral-cure silicone dots inside one upper leg only; the perpendicular leg floats and no adhesive crosses the corner seam",
    "endcap_method": "two tiny removable neutral-cure silicone dots inside the final fascia channel plus a hand pull-check before loading; inspect after every move",
    "qualification": "Every proposed adhesive and fastener must be tested on printed PETG, sealed plywood, and the actual coated steel. Attachment prevents creep, rattle, and falling only; it receives no shelf-load or cargo-restraint credit."
  },
